// Logical path-string utilities: POSIX-only basename/dirname/join + extension
// manipulation. Pure `moonbitlang/core` String API,
// backend-agnostic.
//
// These operate on LOGICAL names (module/package paths, artifact stems) which are
// ALWAYS `/`-separated regardless of OS. For real OS filesystem paths use
// `moonbitlang/x/path` instead — its OS-aware basename/dirname are correct there
// but would mis-split a logical name like `encoding/utf8` on Windows.
